Welcome to Paradise Access Terminal, a restricted system where only authorized users can retrieve classified information. However, there seems to be a vulnerability in how user authentication is handled.

Your mission is to bypass authentication and retrieve the hidden flag stored within the system. Are you ready to break into Paradise?

HINTS

Think about the guest account.

The system has a guest:guest login.

Maybe you can log in as guest and then manipulate the cookies.

Look at how cookies are handled.

The system stores the username in Base64 inside a cookie.

You don’t need to crack passwords—maybe just modify cookies!

💡 Check flag.php?debug=true.

What does this debug mode do? Does it reveal useful information?


💡 Base64 Encoding/Decoding

The system encodes usernames in Base64 (base64_encode($u)).

Can you encode a different username and replace your cookie value?